```
we ensure that the `sk->sk_peer_cred` is properly handled to prevent the use-after-free read flaw. This modification correctly releases the reference to `sk->sk_peer_cred` without the need to acquire `sk->sk_peer_lock`, as it is determined that the current context is the last user of `sk->sk_peer_cred`. This helps in mitigating the vulnerability and ensures proper memory management within the code snippet.

